ion every credible laminate data sheet is written against en 438. knowing how its parts divide up makes the sheets comparable. how the parts of en 438 fit together, which one classifies your product, and how to read a laminate test table — requirement, method and observed value."},{"id":"guide-panel-formats-and-yield","group":"pages","title":"Panel formats and yield: why 4330 × 1830 changes a cut list","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/panel-formats-and-yield","keywords":"panel formats and yield: why 4330 × 1830 changes a cut list format is usually treated as a logistics detail. on a large cut list it is the difference between a viable price and an uncompetitive one. how panel format decides offcut, joint position and decor continuity, with the area figures for each format in the compact and materix programmes."},{"id":"guide-toilet-cubicles-and-lockers","group":"pages","title":"Compact panels for toilet cubicles and lockers: what decides the specification","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/toilet-cubicles-and-lockers","keywords":"compact panels for toilet cubicles and lockers: what decides the specification washrooms and changing rooms are where a surface earns its keep: water at every edge, cleaning chemicals every day and doors that get kicked. the data sheet answers most of it, if it is read in the right order. grade, thickness, moisture, hygiene and hardware — what to settle when specifying compact hpl cubicles, lockers and wet-area partitions, with vault test data."},{"id":"guide-laboratory-worktops","group":"pages","title":"Compact laminate for laboratory worktops: reading chemical-resistance results","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/laboratory-worktops","keywords":"compact laminate for laboratory worktops: reading chemical-resistance results in a laboratory, chemical resistance is not one property. it is a list of substances, each with its own result — and the list is what you need to see. what a sefa 3 chemical resistance result means for a laboratory worktop, how it differs from en 438 staining, and what to ask for before specifying compact hpl."},{"id":"guide-lrv-and-colour-contrast","group":"pages","title":"Light reflectance value (LRV): choosing decors for visual contrast","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/lrv-and-colour-contrast","keywords":"light reflectance value (lrv): choosing decors for visual contrast contrast between a door and its wall, or a worktop and the floor, is what lets people with low vision find their way. lrv turns that into a number you can specify. what lrv measures, why accessibility guidance asks for a 30-point difference between adjacent surfaces, and how to use published lrv figures to choose laminate decors."},{"id":"guide-hygiene-and-food-contact-tests","group":"pages","title":"Antibacterial, antiviral, food-safe: what the laminate test reports actually say","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hygiene-and-food-contact-tests","keywords":"antibacterial, antiviral, food-safe: what the laminate test reports actually say 'antibacterial' and 'food-safe' are claims. behind each one is a specific test with a specific result — and that is what belongs in a specification. jis z 2801, iso 21702, astm g21, en 1186 and en 13130 explained: what each hygiene and food-contact test measures on a laminate surface, and what it cannot prove."},{"id":"guide-hpl-facades-design-review","group":"pages","title":"What architects do with HPL on a façade: a review of the European professional press","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-facades-design-review","keywords":"what architects do with hpl on a façade: a review of the european professional press exterior compact laminate is usually sold on performance. read across the european professional press, it is just as much a design material — and the same sources are clear about where that freedom ends. printed decors, laser-cut reliefs, visible or hidden fixings, balconies and sunshades: what italian and german professional sources show hpl façades can do."},{"id":"guide-hpl-facades-detailing-and-approvals","group":"pages","title":"HPL façades from drawing to site: what the professional press says to check","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-facades-detailing-and-approvals","keywords":"hpl façades from drawing to site: what the professional press says to check the sources agree that an hpl façade succeeds or fails at its details, not in the panel. this is what they say to settle at each stage, from the tender documents to the delivery on site. fixed and sliding points, cavity and fire barriers, ce marking and dop, samples, mock-ups and site acceptance: a checklist compiled from italian and german technical sources."},{"id":"guide-hpl-kitchens-design-review","group":"pages","title":"HPL in the kitchen: what the Italian design press and EuroCucina 2026 show","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-kitchens-design-review","keywords":"hpl in the kitchen: what the italian design press and eurocucina 2026 show italian kitchen makers use hpl for far more than a worktop on a chipboard core. the design press shows where the material is heading; the trade press shows what a thin top asks of the planner. thin compact worktops, sinks made from the same sheet, marble and travertine effects, matching backsplashes: hpl kitchen solutions compiled from italian and german sources."},{"id":"guide-hpl-public-interiors-review","group":"pages","title":"HPL in public interiors: what European technical sources ask of walls, doors and fittings","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-public-interiors-review","keywords":"hpl in public interiors: what european technical sources ask of walls, doors and fittings inside a public building a surface is judged by how it survives cleaning, impact and fire rules, not by how it looks on a sample. the sources below set out those tests — and hpl can be measured against each one. hospitals, schools, transport and hospitality: what italian and german technical sources require of interior surfaces, and how compact and decorative hpl answer it."},{"id":"guide-formaldehyde-limit-2026","group":"pages","title":"Formaldehyde from August 2026: the EU limit for furniture and wood-based articles","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/formaldehyde-limit-2026","keywords":"formaldehyde from august 2026: the eu limit for furniture and wood-based articles reach entry 77 halves the value behind the familiar e1 class and makes it law in every member state. the italian furniture laboratory catas, the trade press and the german environment agency explain what it changes for panel buyers and furniture makers. since 6 august 2026 furniture and wood-based articles in the eu may release at most 0.062 mg/m³ of formaldehyde. what the limit, the test and the exemptions mean."},{"id":"guide-environmental-claims-2026","group":"pages","title":"Environmental claims after 27 September 2026: what furniture and building-product suppliers can still say","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/environmental-claims-2026","keywords":"environmental claims after 27 september 2026: what furniture and building-product suppliers can still say the rules are written for consumer communication, but they reach every supplier whose words end up on a showroom tag or a product page. the italian and german press, a furniture laboratory and a building-products association explain where the line now runs. from 27 september 2026 the eu bans generic 'eco' claims, self-made labels and offset-based climate claims. what the ecgt rules mean for furniture and panel suppliers."},{"id":"guide-construction-products-regulation-2026","group":"pages","title":"The new Construction Products Regulation: what changes for façade and interior panels","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/construction-products-regulation-2026","keywords":"the new construction products regulation: what changes for façade and interior panels the new cpr is in force, but for most product families the familiar declaration of performance and ce marking carry on until new harmonised specifications arrive. the polish building authority, the italian technical press and the eu texts explain the timetable and what to ask for meanwhile. regulation (eu) 2024/3110 has applied since 8 january 2026. declarations of performance and conformity, climate data, digital passports — and why panels still carry a dop."},{"id":"guide-tables-with-compact-tops","group":"pages","title":"Tables with compact tops: what the European furniture standards test","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/tables-with-compact-tops","keywords":"tables with compact tops: what the european furniture standards test a compact laminate top is dense, thin and stiff — but the tests a table must pass are written for the whole table, not the top. italy's furniture laboratory catas explains the methods and the 2023 revisions. stability, top deflection and the 2023 table standards: how en 1730, en 12521 and en 15372 test domestic and contract tables, and what that means for compact tops."},{"id":"guide-ecodesign-for-furniture","group":"pages","title":"Ecodesign for furniture: what the ESPR will ask of furniture makers and their suppliers","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/ecodesign-for-furniture","keywords":"ecodesign for furniture: what the espr will ask of furniture makers and their suppliers the eu has ranked furniture second among the new final products in its first ecodesign working plan. no furniture rules exist yet, but the framework, the timetable and italy's head start show what makers and their panel suppliers should get ready. furniture is a priority under the eu ecodesign for sustainable products regulation, with rules indicatively due in 2028. what may be required and what to prepare now."},{"id":"guide-hpl-or-ceramic-facade","group":"pages","title":"HPL or ceramic on a ventilated façade: what the European sources compare","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-or-ceramic-facade","keywords":"hpl or ceramic on a ventilated façade: what the european sources compare porcelain stoneware and hpl are both common claddings for ventilated façades, and each wins on different ground. italian and german technical sources, a uk government advice note and the façade associations show where. is hpl replacing ceramics on façades? no published data shows it. what the sources do compare: weight, formats, movement, breakage and, above all, fire class."},{"id":"guide-timber-or-wood-look-hpl-facade","group":"pages","title":"Real timber or wood-look HPL on a façade: maintenance, movement and fire","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/timber-or-wood-look-hpl-facade","keywords":"real timber or wood-look hpl on a façade: maintenance, movement and fire wood is back on façades, and so is the question of how it will look in ten years. the german carpentry rules, the swiss timber association lignum and the eu fire classification show what real timber asks of a design — and where a wood-decor laminate is a different answer. timber cladding greys, moves and needs upkeep; wood-decor hpl keeps its colour but is not wood. german, swiss and eu sources compare the two for architects."},{"id":"guide-ventilated-facade-or-etics","group":"pages","title":"Ventilated façade or render on insulation (ETICS): what the European sources compare","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/ventilated-facade-or-etics","keywords":"ventilated façade or render on insulation (etics): what the european sources compare most insulated walls in central and eastern europe are finished with render on insulation boards. germany's environment agency, baunetz wissen and the italian building press explain where that works, where it fails — and what a ventilated façade does differently. etics is cheaper and thinner; a ventilated façade dries better and suits uneven walls. what german and italian sources say about algae, biocides, fire and renovation."},{"id":"guide-hpl-or-aluminium-composite-facade","group":"pages","title":"HPL or aluminium composite on a façade: what the fire rules say after Grenfell","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-or-aluminium-composite-facade","keywords":"hpl or aluminium composite on a façade: what the fire rules say after grenfell aluminium composite panels and hpl compete for the same ventilated façades, and both come in grades that behave very differently in a fire. the official record — the grenfell tower inquiry, the uk government's tests, england's regulations and german building law — shows what separates them. grenfell changed how europe judges façade panels. what the inquiry, the uk government's fire tests, england's bans and german building law say about aluminium composite and hpl."},{"id":"guide-hpl-or-fibre-cement-facade","group":"pages","title":"HPL or fibre cement on a ventilated façade: weight, formats, fire and old asbestos cement","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-or-fibre-cement-facade","keywords":"hpl or fibre cement on a ventilated façade: weight, formats, fire and old asbestos cement fibre cement and hpl are the two board claddings most often hung on ventilated façades. german reference sources, a vienna university thesis and the eu asbestos rules show where they differ — and what applies when the façade being replaced is an old asbestos-cement one. fibre cement is mineral and non-combustible; compact hpl is lighter per millimetre and comes in larger panels. what german sources compare — and what to do with old asbestos-cement cladding."},{"id":"guide-worktops-quartz-porcelain-or-compact","group":"pages","title":"Quartz, porcelain or compact laminate worktops: the silica question for fabricators","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/worktops-quartz-porcelain-or-compact","keywords":"quartz, porcelain or compact laminate worktops: the silica question for fabricators worktops are chosen for looks, heat and scratch resistance. for the people who cut them there is another question: crystalline silica. spain's national occupational-safety institute, the veneto region's health service and eu law show why quartz agglomerate needs particular care in the workshop — and where porcelain and compact laminate stand. cutting quartz agglomerate has caused a wave of silicosis among worktop fabricators in spain and italy. what the health authorities report, what the eu limit is, and where porcelain and compact laminate stand."},{"id":"guide-rushil-compact-test-margins","group":"pages","title":"Above the minimum: what Rushil's compact laminate test reports show","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/rushil-compact-test-margins","keywords":"above the minimum: what rushil's compact laminate test reports show every compliant compact laminate meets en 438. the better question for a specifier is how much margin there is above it. rushil's data sheets answer with figures — and in several properties the margin is large. en 438 sets the floor. rushil's published data show how far above it its compact laminate tests — strength, impact, wear, water, weathering and fire, figure by figure."},{"id":"guide-rushil-compact-international-tests","group":"pages","title":"One panel, many rulebooks: the international tests behind Rushil compact laminate","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/rushil-compact-international-tests","keywords":"one panel, many rulebooks: the international tests behind rushil compact laminate rushil decor sells in more than 57 countries, and a panel that crosses borders meets a different rulebook at each one. the company has had its compact laminates tested to european, american, british and japanese methods — and publishes the reports. europe's en 13501 and en 16516, america's astm e84, ul 94, nsf/ansi 35 and fda rules, california's cdph method, britain's bs 476, japan's jis z 2801 — and rushil's results in each."},{"id":"guide-sottsass-memphis-laminate","group":"pages","title":"Sottsass, Memphis and laminate: how a kitchen-counter material entered the design museum","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/sottsass-memphis-laminate","keywords":"sottsass, memphis and laminate: how a kitchen-counter material entered the design museum in 1981 a group of milan designers covered their furniture in printed laminate and changed the course of design. their pieces now stand in the metropolitan museum of art and the national gallery of victoria — and the museums' own texts explain why the material mattered. ettore sottsass and the memphis group made printed plastic laminate the face of 1980s design. what the met, the national gallery of victoria and the designers themselves say about it."},{"id":"guide-gehry-venturi-laminate","group":"pages","title":"Two Pritzker laureates and laminate: Frank Gehry's fish lamps and Venturi Scott Brown's chairs","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/gehry-venturi-laminate","keywords":"two pritzker laureates and laminate: frank gehry's fish lamps and venturi scott brown's chairs two of the most celebrated architects of the late 20th century took laminate seriously. frank gehry turned its shards into glowing fish; robert venturi and denise scott brown printed a pattern on it and wrapped chairs in it. museums from san francisco to london keep the results. in 1983 a laminate maker invited architects to experiment. frank gehry broke a sheet and made fish lamps that museums now collect; venturi scott brown wrapped chairs in a printed laminate that moma and the v&a keep."},{"id":"guide-hpl-tops-design-classics","group":"pages","title":"Aalto, Prouvé and the Eameses: the design classics their makers top with HPL","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-tops-design-classics","keywords":"aalto, prouvé and the eameses: the design classics their makers top with hpl few pieces of furniture are as carefully kept as the classics of modern design. the companies that make them today decide which materials are good enough for the originals — and for tables by alvar aalto, jean prouvé and charles and ray eames, high-pressure laminate is on the short list. artek and vitra still make tables designed by alvar aalto, jean prouvé and charles and ray eames — and each offers them with a high-pressure laminate top. what the makers say about the material."},{"id":"guide-compact-hpl-grcic-bouroullec-morrison","group":"pages","title":"Grcic, the Bouroullecs and Jasper Morrison: compact HPL in today's design tables","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/compact-hpl-grcic-bouroullec-morrison","keywords":"grcic, the bouroullecs and jasper morrison: compact hpl in today's design tables some of the best-known designers working today put their tables on a top of solid compact laminate. konstantin grcic's tables for plank and vitra's tables by the bouroullec brothers and jasper morrison all offer a self-supporting hpl top 10 or 12 mm thick, made to go outdoors. konstantin grcic's tables for plank and tables by ronan and erwan bouroullec and jasper morrison for vitra come with 10–12 mm compact hpl tops for indoor and outdoor use. what the makers say, and where the limits are."},{"id":"guide-cleaning-hpl-surfaces","group":"pages","title":"Cleaning HPL and compact surfaces: what the industry guidance says","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/cleaning-hpl-surfaces","keywords":"cleaning hpl and compact surfaces: what the industry guidance says hpl needs little care, but it is not indestructible. europe's laminate manufacturers publish one cleaning guide for the whole material. this is what it says, stain by stain. daily cleaning, limescale, wax, paint, glue and silicone: how to clean hpl and compact laminate, by the guidance of europe's decorative laminates industry."},{"id":"guide-machining-compact-hpl","group":"pages","title":"Machining compact HPL: sawing, milling, drilling and fixing","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/machining-compact-hpl","keywords":"machining compact hpl: sawing, milling, drilling and fixing compact hpl is worked on ordinary woodworking machines, but it is denser and harder than any board, and it moves with the climate. the industry's processing leaflet gives the numbers that decide a clean cut and a sound fixing. feed per tooth, edge allowance, drill angles, oversized holes and tongue-and-groove sizes: how to work compact hpl, by the guidance of europe's hpl industry."},{"id":"guide-hpl-in-wet-rooms","group":"pages","title":"HPL and compact in bathrooms and wet rooms: cores, edges and joints","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-in-wet-rooms","keywords":"hpl and compact in bathrooms and wet rooms: cores, edges and joints hpl has decades of use in bathrooms, showers and changing rooms. whether a wall or a vanity unit lasts depends less on the laminate than on what is behind it: the core board, the glue line and every edge. which boards, adhesives, edges and joints suit hpl in dry rooms, splash zones and wet rooms — and where only compact will do, by the guidance of europe's hpl industry."},{"id":"guide-hpl-hospital-hygiene-research","group":"pages","title":"HPL in healthcare: what infection-control research has measured","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-hospital-hygiene-research","keywords":"hpl in healthcare: what infection-control research has measured hospitals treat surfaces as part of infection control. a handful of peer-reviewed studies have put high-pressure laminate under the microscope. this is what they found, the favourable and the less so. mrsa survival, wear, disinfection and hand transfer: what peer-reviewed studies from the us, sweden, portugal and germany measured on laminate surfaces."},{"id":"guide-compact-hpl-materials-research","group":"pages","title":"Compact HPL in materials research: strength, joints and cure","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/compact-hpl-materials-research","keywords":"compact hpl in materials research: strength, joints and cure compact hpl is sold on strength and durability. furniture engineers and materials scientists have measured what lies behind those words, and where the material still depends on how it is worked. bending strength against mdf, particleboard and plywood, glued corner joints, cutting forces and resin cure: compact hpl as peer-reviewed research measured it."},{"id":"guide-hpl-in-particle-detectors","group":"pages","title":"HPL at CERN: the laminate inside the particle detectors","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-in-particle-detectors","keywords":"hpl at cern: the laminate inside the particle detectors the material family that faces a kitchen worktop lines thousands of square metres of particle detectors at cern. physics journals explain how it is used, and what that says about hpl. cms and atlas at cern detect muons with resistive plate chambers built from hpl electrodes. what physics papers say about the material and what it is asked to do."},{"id":"guide-hpl-in-research-labs","group":"pages","title":"Why researchers build with HPL: bone models, sound absorbers, test rigs","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-in-research-labs","keywords":"why researchers build with hpl: bone models, sound absorbers, test rigs hpl turns up in laboratories that have nothing to do with furniture. read across the research literature, the reasons are the ones that make it a good worktop: known stiffness, flatness and easy machining. surgeons, acousticians, building scientists and engineers use hpl in their experiments. what seven peer-reviewed studies used it for, and which properties they relied on."},{"id":"guide-greener-hpl-research","group":"pages","title":"Greener HPL: lignin, sugar-based resins and a second life for waste","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/greener-hpl-research","keywords":"greener hpl: lignin, sugar-based resins and a second life for waste hpl owes much of its toughness to fossil-based phenolic resin, and making it takes energy. laboratories in europe, the americas and asia are working on both ends of the problem. this is how far they have got. lignin in place of phenol, a sugar-based resin on recycled kraft paper, waste turned into hydrogen-rich gas: what peer-reviewed research shows about a greener hpl."},{"id":"guide-machining-compact-research","group":"pages","title":"Machining compact HPL: what cutting research measured","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/machining-compact-research","keywords":"machining compact hpl: what cutting research measured industry leaflets say how to cut compact hpl. machining researchers in poland, the czech republic and turkey measured why: the forces, the surface finish and the damage a worn tool leaves behind. cutting resistance, climb versus conventional milling, and drilling with new and worn tools: what three peer-reviewed studies measured when machining hpl and compact."},{"id":"guide-hpl-surface-science","group":"pages","title":"The HPL surface under the microscope: cracks, stains and fingerprints","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-surface-science","keywords":"the hpl surface under the microscope: cracks, stains and fingerprints the melamine surface is the part of hpl everyone touches. materials scientists have studied how it forms, when it cracks and how it can be made to shed stains and fingerprints. this is what they found. why laminates crack, how melamine resin cures, and what additives do for stains and fingerprints: what peer-reviewed surface research on hpl has measured."},{"id":"guide-laminate-surfaces-formaldehyde-research","group":"pages","title":"Laminate surfaces and formaldehyde: what emission research measured","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/laminate-surfaces-formaldehyde-research","keywords":"laminate surfaces and formaldehyde: what emission research measured most of the formaldehyde in furniture comes from the board inside, not the surface outside. emission researchers have measured how much a laminate surface holds back, and where it lets go. melamine-faced boards, pvc film and sealed edges in emission chambers: what peer-reviewed studies found about surfaces, edges and formaldehyde, and what it means for hpl."},{"id":"guide-hpl-wear-scratch-resistance-research","group":"pages","title":"HPL against daily wear: what abrasion and scratch studies measured","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-wear-scratch-resistance-research","keywords":"hpl against daily wear: what abrasion and scratch studies measured desks, counters and cabinet fronts are judged by how they look after years of use. laboratory studies from türkiye and norway have measured how hpl resists abrasion and scratching, and what makes one surface tougher than another. hpl beat veneer, cpl and foil on scratch and abrasion, and an aluminium oxide overlay raised wear resistance 35-fold: what laboratory studies measured."},{"id":"guide-hpl-facades-summer-heat-flow","group":"pages","title":"HPL façades in summer: what heat-flow research has measured","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-facades-summer-heat-flow","keywords":"hpl façades in summer: what heat-flow research has measured a ventilated façade is the building's sunshade. researchers in barcelona have measured and modelled one clad in hpl, and found that the colour of the panels, the air gap behind them and the wall beneath decide whether summer heat gets in. in a validated model, colour alone moved an hpl-clad façade from heat gain to heat loss on a summer day, and researchers favour low-conductivity claddings."},{"id":"guide-hpl-heat-steam-resistance-research","group":"pages","title":"HPL and kitchen heat: what dry-heat, steam and burn tests measured","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-heat-steam-resistance-research","keywords":"hpl and kitchen heat: what dry-heat, steam and burn tests measured a kitchen or bar counter meets hot dishes, steam and the occasional cigarette. laboratory studies from türkiye and portugal have put high-pressure laminate through the standard heat tests, and the melamine surface comes out well. standard hpl took 180 °c for 20 minutes without visible change, and an aluminium oxide overlay lifted cigarette-burn resistance from grade 2 to 5."},{"id":"guide-eudr-and-hpl-2026","group":"pages","title":"EUDR from 30 December 2026: where HPL and compact laminate stand","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/eudr-and-hpl-2026","keywords":"eudr from 30 december 2026: where hpl and compact laminate stand from 30 december 2026, wood, paper and wooden furniture can be placed on the eu market only with a due diligence statement. here is what the regulation lists, where high-pressure laminate sits in the customs tariff, and what that means for panels and furniture made with it. the eu deforestation regulation applies from 30 december 2026. hpl is classified under cn 3921 90 41, outside annex i; hpl-faced boards and wooden furniture are in."},{"id":"guide-food-business-worktops-eu-law","group":"pages","title":"Worktops in food businesses: what EU hygiene and food-contact law asks","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/food-business-worktops-eu-law","keywords":"worktops in food businesses: what eu hygiene and food-contact law asks restaurants, canteens and food shops answer to two sets of eu rules: one on hygiene, one on materials that touch food. read together, they describe the ideal worktop, and a compact laminate tested against them fits the description. eu hygiene law asks for smooth, washable, corrosion-resistant, non-toxic surfaces; food-contact law judges repeated-use materials on the third migration test."},{"id":"guide-whole-life-carbon-epbd-epd","group":"pages","title":"Whole-life carbon from 2028: why façade and interior panels need an EPD","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/whole-life-carbon-epbd-epd","keywords":"whole-life carbon from 2028: why façade and interior panels need an epd the recast energy performance of buildings directive makes the carbon footprint of a whole building part of its energy performance certificate. that calculation runs on product data, and an environmental product declaration is how a panel supplies it. from 2028 the recast epbd puts life-cycle gwp on the energy certificate of new buildings over 1,000 m², using product-specific data where it is available."},{"id":"guide-healthcare-walls-washrooms-hbn","group":"pages","title":"Hospital walls and washrooms: what NHS design guidance asks of surfaces, and where compact fits","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/healthcare-walls-washrooms-hbn","keywords":"hospital walls and washrooms: what nhs design guidance asks of surfaces, and where compact fits health building note 00-10 sets out what the walls, ceilings and sanitary assemblies of healthcare buildings should be made of. read clause by clause, its requirements describe a compact laminate. hbn 00-10 asks for smooth, seamless, impervious walls that resist knocks, detergents and microbial growth. vault's published results answer each point."},{"id":"guide-hpl-stain-chemical-resistance-research","group":"pages","title":"Coffee, ink and caustic soda: what stain tests on HPL have measured","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-stain-chemical-resistance-research","keywords":"coffee, ink and caustic soda: what stain tests on hpl have measured a worktop, a desk or a hospital wall meets coffee, wine, ink, cleaners and disinfectants. laboratory studies and the en 438 staining test show how the melamine surface of hpl stands up to them. citric acid, caustic soda and hydrogen peroxide left no mark on any hpl tested in türkiye, and an aluminium oxide overlay lifted ink resistance from grade 2 to 5."},{"id":"guide-pool-halls-changing-rooms-compact","group":"pages","title":"Pool halls and changing rooms: why compact suits one of the harshest indoor climates","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/pool-halls-changing-rooms-compact","keywords":"pool halls and changing rooms: why compact suits one of the harshest indoor climates swimming pools combine heat, humidity and chlorine chemistry as few buildings do. britain's safety regulator has documented what that air does to metal; here is what it means for cubicles, lockers and benches. warm, humid, chloramine-laden air makes indoor pools one of the most aggressive building atmospheres. compact hpl panels contain no metal to corrode."},{"id":"guide-fsc-pefc-certified-hpl","group":"pages","title":"FSC® and PEFC™ certified HPL: what Rushil's certificates cover and how to order it","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/fsc-pefc-certified-hpl","keywords":"fsc® and pefc™ certified hpl: what rushil's certificates cover and how to order it hpl is mostly paper, and paper comes from forests. since september 2025 rushil can supply its laminates with an fsc or pefc claim. here is what the two certificates cover, what the claims mean, and how to order so that the claim reaches your invoice. rushil holds fsc and pefc chain-of-custody certificates for its laminates, valid to 2030. what the claims mean and how to get certified hpl on your invoice."},{"id":"guide-hpl-gloss-levels-finishes","group":"pages","title":"High gloss, semi-gloss, suede or matt: choosing an HPL finish","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-gloss-levels-finishes","keywords":"high gloss, semi-gloss, suede or matt: choosing an hpl finish the same decor can look deep and reflective or soft and quiet, depending on its finish. with hpl that finish is formed in the press and is part of the cured surface. here is how gloss is measured, what the standard asks of each finish, and how to choose. gloss is pressed into an hpl surface, not painted on. how the four finishes are measured, what en 438 asks of each and how rushil's surfaces perform."},{"id":"guide-how-hpl-is-made","group":"pages","title":"How HPL is made: from kraft paper to compact panel","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/how-hpl-is-made","keywords":"how hpl is made: from kraft paper to compact panel high-pressure laminate starts as rolls of paper and ends as a surface that shrugs off heat, water and wear. the process is simple to describe and exacting to run. here it is step by step, with where rushil's products fit. paper, resin, heat and pressure: how high-pressure laminate is made, step by step, and how rushil's decorative, compact and exterior grades are built."},{"id":"guide-iso-9001-14001-45001-certificates","group":"pages","title":"ISO 9001, 14001 and 45001: what Rushil's management certificates tell a buyer","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/iso-9001-14001-45001-certificates","keywords":"iso 9001, 14001 and 45001: what rushil's management certificates tell a buyer a laminate is judged by its test results, and those results are only as good as the factory that repeats them sheet after sheet. that is what management-system certificates are about. here is what rushil's three certificates cover, how to verify them, and what the new 2026 editions of iso 9001 and iso 14001 mean. rushil's management system has been certified since 2007, now to iso 9001, 14001 and 45001. what it covers, how to check it and what iso 9001:2026 changes."},{"id":"guide-melamine-reach-candidate-list-hpl","group":"pages","title":"Melamine on the REACH Candidate List: what it means for HPL","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/melamine-reach-candidate-list-hpl","keywords":"melamine on the reach candidate list: what it means for hpl the melamine resin that gives hpl its hard, cleanable surface is made from a substance the eu now lists as being of very high concern. buyers ask what that means. in short, the duties depend on how much melamine as such is in a product, and rushil's topaz screening puts every listed substance at or below the threshold. melamine became an eu substance of very high concern in 2023. what that means for laminates, who must inform whom, and what rushil's topaz screening shows."},{"id":"guide-eu-india-trade-agreement-hpl","group":"pages","title":"The EU–India trade agreement and HPL: what changes for buyers, and what to check","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/eu-india-trade-agreement-hpl","keywords":"the eu–india trade agreement and hpl: what changes for buyers, and what to check the free trade agreement between the eu and india is on its way to signature, and europe's laminate industry is watching closely. lower tariffs would not change the rules any laminate must meet in europe. here is where the deal stands, what the industry worries about, and how to check a laminate made in india against each concern. the eu–india deal will cut tariffs once in force; europe's laminate makers want strict import checks. what buyers should verify, with rushil's answers."},{"id":"guide-wet-room-walls-compact-or-tiles","group":"pages","title":"Wet-room walls: compact panels or ceramic tiles?","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/wet-room-walls-compact-or-tiles","keywords":"wet-room walls: compact panels or ceramic tiles? tiles are the default for showers and washrooms, and the tile itself is not the problem. the joints are. a swedish research institute opened up bathroom walls to see what happens behind the tiles; here is what it found, and why large compact panels change the picture. water wicks through grout into tiled walls and takes months to dry. a swedish study found microbes behind tiles in 13 bathrooms. compact panels avoid joints."},{"id":"guide-how-long-does-hpl-last","group":"pages","title":"How long does HPL last? Service life, and why it counts for carbon","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/how-long-does-hpl-last","keywords":"how long does hpl last? service life, and why it counts for carbon a surface that has to be replaced is bought, made and fitted twice. that is why service life is becoming a number designers ask for, not a sales phrase. here is what the laminate industry says about how long hpl lasts, why it now counts in carbon calculations, and what rushil's tests show about the wear behind it. the laminate industry expects hpl to last 20 to 50 years. why that matters now eu buildings must report whole-life carbon, and what rushil's tests add."},{"id":"guide-hpl-light-fastness-colour","group":"pages","title":"Will the colour last? Light fastness of HPL compared with wood","meta":"Technical guides","href":"/guides/hpl-light-fastness-colour","keywords":"will the colour last? light fastness of hpl compared with wood wood changes colour in light: it yellows, darkens or fades, even indoors under ordinary lamps. for many uses that is part of its charm. where a colour has to stay as specified, a printed hpl decor is built to hold it. here is what the research on wood shows, how light fastness is tested, and what rushil's laminates achieve. wood changes colour even under indoor lamps; hpl decors are built to hold theirs. what wood research shows, how light fastness is tested and rushil's results."},{"id":"page-/technical","group":"pages","title":"technical.title","href":"/technical","keywords":"technical.title /technical"},{"id":"page-/technical/fire","group":"pages","title":"Fire","href":"/technical/fire","keywords":"fire /technical/fire"},{"id":"page-/technical/food-contact","group":"pages","title":"Food contact","href":"/technical/food-contact","keywords":"food contact /technical/food-contact"},{"id":"page-/technical/indoor-air","group":"pages","title":"Indoor air","href":"/technical/indoor-air","keywords":"indoor air /technical/indoor-air"},{"id":"page-/technical/care-maintenance","group":"pages","title":"Care & maintenance","href":"/technical/care-maintenance","keywords":"care & maintenance /technical/care-maintenance"},{"id":"page-/technical/sustainability","group":"pages","title":"Certification","href":"/technical/sustainability","keywords":"certification /technical/sustainability"},{"id":"page-/downloads","group":"pages","title":"Downloads","href":"/downloads","keywords":"downloads /downloads"},{"id":"page-/decors","group":"pages","title":"Decor explorer","href":"/decors","keywords":"decor explorer /decors"},{"id"